course: dictionary
lesson: 11966
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A catechism is a short summary of the main beliefs of a Christian church, set out as questions and answers. It is used to teach the faith, so people learn it in church lessons.
explain: «Mia spent every Saturday learning the catechism before her First Communion.» The clues are church, learning and a special event. So catechism here means the beliefs taught in church lessons.
explain: The same word can also mean a set of questions asked one after another, like a test. «The quiz master fired a catechism of quick questions at the class.» Here there is no church. The clue is quick questions, one after another. Try the meaning in the sentence to check: a quick set of questions fits, so this is the second meaning.
fact: A catechism is a summary of a church's main beliefs, set out as questions and answers.
fact: «Catechism class» is a lesson where children or new members learn the beliefs of their faith.
fact: Church phrases you may meet include «learn the catechism» and «the Catholic catechism».
fact: A catechism can also be any set of questions asked one after another, like a test.
fact: When a word has two meanings, the words around it tell you which meaning the writer chose.
exercise: «Ella goes to catechism class on Saturdays.» What is a catechism class? | A lesson in cooking | A library for old books | A sports club with a ball and a whistle | *A lesson where children learn the beliefs of their church
exercise: «The quiz master read out a catechism of quick questions, one after another.» What does catechism mean here? | A church service with singing | A long story told at night | *A set of questions asked one after another, like a test | A kind of bread
exercise: «Mia learned the catechism before her First Communion.» Which word is the clue that this is about church? | learned | before | *Communion | catechism
test: «Anya will be confirmed next year, so she is in her catechism class.» What does catechism class mean? | A class about the weather | A class for learning to swim | *A lesson on the beliefs of her faith | A class for painting pictures
test: «The teacher asked the catechism questions, and the children answered together.» What kind of catechism is this? | A painting of a saint | A type of candle | A church song | *A set of questions asked one after another, like a test
exam: «Each child answered the catechism from memory.» What does catechism mean in this sentence? | A type of candle | A long church song | A painting of a saint | *Questions and answers that teach church beliefs
